<H1 style=3D"WIDTH: 70%">DFSMSrmm Catalog Synchronization</H1><IMG=20
alt=3D"Redbooks logo" =
src=3D"http://www.redbooks.ibm.com/Redbooks.nsf/rb170x32.gif">=20
</DIV><!-- TITLE_END --><!-- CONTENT_BODY -->
<DIV id=3Dibm-content-body>
<DIV id=3Dibm-content-main>
<DIV class=3Dibm-intro id=3Dibm-leadspace><IMG height=3D5 alt=3D""=20
src=3D"http://www.ibm.com/images/common/bluebar.gif" width=3D"100%" =
border=3D0> </DIV>
<DIV class=3Dibm-container>
<H2>Abstract</H2>
<DIV class=3Dibm-container-body>
<P>In this Technote we describe how DFSMSrmm Catalog Synchronization can =
be used=20
to synchronize your MVS user catalogs with DFSMSrmm to reduce catalog =
locates.=20
</P></DIV></DIV><A name=3Dcontents></A>
<DIV class=3Dibm-container>
<H2>Contents</H2>
<DIV class=3Dibm-container-body>
<P>
<DIV class=3Dibm-domino-rtf>
<P><B><FONT face=3DArial>Catalog synchronization</FONT></B>=20
<P><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>When you run DFSMSrmm with user catalogs =
and the=20
DFSMSrmm control data set unsynchronized, DFSMSrmm issues catalog =
locates as=20
required to check if data sets are cataloged. Catalog locates use the =
standard=20
catalog search to find if a data set is cataloged. Any data sets =
cataloged using=20
JOBCAT or STEPCAT might not be found to be cataloged, because the =
standard=20
catalog search might not find them.</FONT>=20
<P><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>When you enable catalog synchronization, =
DFSMSrmm=20
synchronizes the DFSMSrmm control data set and available user catalogs. =
Enabling=20
catalog synchronization is normally a one-time task. Once the catalog =
status is=20
synchronized, DFSMSrmm continually tracks and updates the catalog =
status. When=20
you run DFSMSrmm with user catalogs and the DFSMSrmm control data set=20
synchronized, DFSMSrmm does not need to issue catalog locates to find if =
a data=20
set is cataloged. The catalog status tracked by DFSMSrmm in the control =
data set=20
is used to determine if a data set is cataloged. When DFSMSrmm tracks =
catalog=20
status, it does so regardless of whether JOBCAT or STEPCAT is used. =
During=20
catalog synchronization, DFSMSrmm uses the Catalog Search Interface =
(CSI) to=20
retrieve data set catalog information. CSI returns catalog information =
for all=20
data sets in all catalogs that are in or connected to the master =
catalog.=20
Because of this, DFSMSrmm can detect that a data set is cataloged even =
if it=20
cannot be found using the standard catalog search.</FONT>=20
<P><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>If you have switched on catalog =
synchronization, you=20
do not need shared ICF-user catalogs to retain tape data sets as long as =
they=20
are cataloged. If you have unshared ICF-user catalogs you have to split =
your=20
daily inventory management. This is because you have to run the =
expiration=20
processing on each system that has unshared ICF-user catalogs to return =
expired=20
volumes back to scratch status. </FONT><BR>
<P><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>You enable catalog synchronization by =
specifying the=20
DFSMSrmm EDGRMMxx OPTION CATSYSID operand. When you specify the CATSYSID =

operand, DFSMSrmm uses the catalog search interface to obtain catalog=20
information used for DFSMSrmm vital record processing. DFSMSrmm performs =

checking to determine that the catalog search interface catalog =
environment does=20
not have any errors that might prevent successful processing. DFSMSrmm =
issues=20
messages EDG2235E, EDG2236I, or EDG2237E when an error is encountered. =
If you do=20
not specify the DFSMSrmm EDGRMMxx OPTION CATSYSID operand, DFSMSrmm =
vital record=20
processing uses catalog locates to determine if data sets are still =
cataloged.=20
</FONT>
<P><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>You must re-synchronize the DFSMSrmm =
control data set=20
and user catalogs under these conditions: </FONT>
<UL>
  <LI type=3Ddisc><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>You ran EDGHSKP with =
CATSYNCH and=20
  VERIFY, and differences in catalog status were found. DFSMSrmm clears =
the=20
  catalog synchronization date and time to force you to run CATSYNCH. =
</FONT>
  <LI type=3Ddisc><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>DFSMSrmm is not active =
when catalog=20
  activity for tape data sets is taking place. DFSMSrmm issues messages =
EDG8200E=20
  and EDG8201E when DFSMSrmm cannot track catalog updates. </FONT>
  <LI type=3Ddisc><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>A DFSMSrmm failure occurs =
during catalog=20
  processing. DFSMSrmm issues messages EDG8200E and EDG8201E when an =
error is=20
  detected in processing. </FONT>
  <LI type=3Ddisc><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>You connect or disconnect =
user catalogs=20
  (that contain entries for tape data sets) to the master=20
catalog.</FONT></LI></UL><BR><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>When you use =
IDCAMS REPRO=20
MERGECAT for catalog maintenance, you do not need to run a job to =
re-synchronize=20
the DFSMSrmm control data set and catalogs.</FONT><FONT face=3DArial =
size=3D2>=20
</FONT></DIV>
<P></P></DIV></DIV>
<P></P>
